        "v": 5,
        "title": "CI now runs tests and LLM APIs move to llm-apis directory",
        "summary": "CI workflow `build-and-typecheck` renamed to `build-and-test`, replacing sequential package builds with `bun run typecheck` and adding `bun test` steps for npm-app, backend, and common. Backend LLM modules (`claude`, `gemini-with-fallbacks`) moved to `src/llm-apis/`; `common/actions` imports replaced by `common/types/message`. `knowledge.md` exclusion removed from file request prompts, allowing knowledge files in context. `SWELancer-Benchmark` submodule and `conversation-progress.ts` deleted.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T16:51:31.682Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The project's automated testing system now actually runs the code's tests instead of just checking if it compiles. Previously, when developers submitted changes, the system only verified the code was valid but never executed the actual tests; now it runs the test suites for the main components to catch bugs before they reach production. The behind-the-scenes file organization was also tidied up, with AI model integrations moved into a dedicated folder, though this has no visible impact on how the software behaves for users.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
