        "summary": "Version bumped from 1.0.169 to 1.0.170 in npm-app/package.json. This is a patch release, typically containing minor fixes or internal updates.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T23:41:09.911Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The app you install just got its version label updated to 1.0.170, which bundles several fixes and tweaks made over the past couple of weeks. Since yesterday, you can stop the assistant mid-task after it used its tools six times without it forcing a pause, and the free plan now caps your monthly credits at 500. Behind the scenes, the system now runs its checking and test steps on every new code push, and the limits that control how much the assistant thinks before it answers have been adjusted, so responses behave a bit more predictably. If you look, you'd see these changes took effect as soon as you installed the latest version.",
